# Applies to builds whose context is the repo root (codex / claudecode
# derived images per agent_decoupling/06_design.md §4.2). The legacy kali
# base build uses context=agent/kali/ and is unaffected.
#
# CRITICAL: this file is created BEFORE the first repo-root COPY in any
# Dockerfile. A .dockerignore added AFTER a layer is built does not
# retroact on history; the secret would be permanently in the published image.

# --- Secrets (blocking) ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/credentials.json
**/secrets.json
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.aws/
**/.netrc
**/.ssh/

# Explicit: agent/.env exists on operator hosts and is read by
# agent/custom_agent.py via load_dotenv. Never bake into images.
agent/.env

# --- Bloat (excludes large/irrelevant trees from the build context) ---
.git/
logs/
lab/
research/
documentation/
.obsidian/
RELEASE_READINESS.md
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo

# Apps' built artifacts (recompiled at runtime if needed)
apps/*/exploit/
apps/*/apk/
